---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro'
import SiteFooter from '../components/SiteFooter.astro'
import { formatLastUpdated } from '../lib/legal'

// Bump when the wording below changes in substance. `pnpm check-legal-dates` fails the
// build if this page is committed with a date older than the commit touching it.
const LAST_UPDATED = '2026-09-04'
---

<BaseLayout
    title="Privacy Policy"
    description="Privacy Policy for Modrex, the free and open-source desktop mod manager."
>
    <Nav />
    <main class="legal-page">
        <div class="wrap">
            <div class="prose">
                <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
                <p class="updated">Last updated: {formatLastUpdated(LAST_UPDATED)}</p>

                <p>
                    Modrex is built to respect your privacy. This policy covers both the Modrex
                    desktop app and this website (modrex.net).
                </p>

                <h2>Desktop app</h2>
                <p>
                    Modrex does not collect any data by default. The app includes an optional,
                    opt-in analytics feature:
                </p>
                <ul>
                    <li>
                        <strong>Opt-in only.</strong> You are asked once on first launch and can change
                        your choice at any time in Settings.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <strong>What is collected if you opt in:</strong> anonymous usage events (features
                        used, mods installed, app version, operating system). A random per-install ID
                        is generated locally — it is never linked to your name, email, or any account.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <strong>What is never collected:</strong> file paths, the text you type into mod
                        search (only its length), game save data, your account credentials, or your name
                        or email address.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <strong>Processor, and your IP address:</strong> analytics events are sent to
                        Google Analytics 4 through a proxy at modrex.net, running on Cloudflare Pages.
                        The proxy reads the IP address your connection arrives from and forwards it to
                        Google in the same request, so that country-level statistics reflect where you
                        are rather than where the proxy is. The proxy does not store it and Modrex keeps
                        no database of it. An IP address can count as personal data in some jurisdictions,
                        so it is disclosed here even though it is used only for approximate location.
                        See <a
                            href="https://policies.google.com/privacy"
                            target="_blank"
                            rel="noopener">Google's Privacy Policy</a
                        >.
                    </li>
                </ul>
                <p>
                    If you opt out (or never opt in), the app sends no analytics at all, and no IP
                    address reaches modrex.net or Google from it.
                </p>

                <h2>Services Modrex contacts</h2>
                <p>
                    Modrex is a desktop app, so ordinary use means talking to a handful of services.
                    Besides the mod sites you browse, ModWorkshop and Nexus Mods, a normal session
                    reaches:
                </p>
                <ul>
                    <li>
                        <strong>GitHub</strong>, to check whether a newer Modrex release exists and
                        to download it when you choose to update.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <strong>index.modrex.net</strong>, to download the mod-identification index
                        that lets Modrex recognize mods already in your game folder.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <strong>Steam's public content network</strong>, for the cover art shown on
                        the game picker.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <strong>paydaythegame.com</strong>, for the in-app news tab, on the games
                        that have one.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <strong>The download host a mod loader is published on</strong>, when you
                        install a loader, and <strong
                            >the update address a mod itself declares</strong
                        >, when Modrex checks that mod for a newer version. These hosts are chosen
                        by the loader and mod authors, not by Modrex.
                    </li>
                </ul>
                <p>
                    None of these carry an account identifier or the anonymous analytics ID. Like
                    any request your computer makes, each one reveals your IP address to the service
                    it goes to, under that service's own privacy policy.
                </p>

                <h2>Nexus Mods sign-in (optional)</h2>
                <p>
                    Modrex can browse and install mods from Nexus Mods. That requires signing in to
                    your Nexus Mods account, which happens in your own browser using Nexus's OAuth
                    flow. Modrex never sees or handles your Nexus Mods password.
                </p>
                <ul>
                    <li>
                        <strong>What is stored:</strong> the access token and refresh token that Nexus
                        issues, plus the time the access token expires. No password and no profile information
                        is stored.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <strong>Where it is stored:</strong> in your operating system's credential store
                        (Windows Credential Manager, or a Secret Service provider such as gnome-keyring
                        or KWallet on Linux). Only the expiry time is written to Modrex's own settings
                        file.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <strong>Where it is sent:</strong> only to Nexus Mods, to authorize your own requests
                        to their API. These tokens are never transmitted to modrex.net or to any other
                        server operated by Modrex.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <strong>On Linux with no credential store:</strong> if no Secret Service provider
                        is running, Modrex falls back to storing both tokens in plain text in its configuration
                        file (<code>~/.config/modrex/settings.json</code>), where other users of the
                        same computer may be able to read them. Modrex shows a warning in Settings
                        whenever this is the case. Installing and enabling gnome-keyring or KWallet
                        and restarting Modrex moves the tokens into the credential store.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <strong>Removing it:</strong> signing out in Settings deletes both tokens from
                        the credential store and from the settings file.
                    </li>
                </ul>
                <p>
                    Your use of Nexus Mods is also governed by their own <a
                        href="https://help.nexusmods.com/article/20-privacy-policy"
                        target="_blank"
                        rel="noopener">Privacy Policy</a
                    >.
                </p>

                <h2>Website (modrex.net)</h2>
                <p>
                    This website uses Google Analytics 4 with Consent Mode v2. Analytics are denied
                    by default and only enabled if you accept via the cookie banner. We do not use
                    any other tracking, advertising networks, or third-party data brokers.
                </p>

                <h2>Data sharing</h2>
                <p>
                    We do not sell, rent, or trade any data. We do not share data with third parties
                    except as required by the analytics processor described above or by law. Nexus
                    Mods sign-in tokens are never shared with anyone: they stay on your device and
                    go only to Nexus Mods itself.
                </p>

                <h2>Changes</h2>
                <p>
                    We may update this policy at any time. The "Last updated" date above will
                    reflect any changes.
                </p>

                <h2>Contact</h2>
                <p>
                    Questions? Open an issue on <a
                        href="https://github.com/modrexio/modrex/issues"
                        target="_blank"
                        rel="noopener">GitHub</a
                    > or join our <a
                        href="https://discord.gg/tenzpx8JRM"
                        target="_blank"
                        rel="noopener">Discord</a
                    >.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </main>
    <SiteFooter />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
    .legal-page {
        padding: 80px 0 96px;
    }

    .prose {
        max-width: 680px;
    }

    h1 {
        margin: 0 0 24px;
        font-family: var(--font-display);
        font-size: clamp(36px, 5vw, 56px);
        line-height: 1;
        letter-spacing: var(--tracking-display);
    }

    .updated {
        margin: -12px 0 24px;
        font-size: 12px;
        font-weight: 600;
        color: var(--color-text);
    }

    h2 {
        margin: 40px 0 10px;
        font-size: 16px;
        font-weight: 600;
        color: var(--color-text);
    }

    code {
        font-family: var(--font-mono);
        font-size: 13px;
        color: var(--color-text);
        overflow-wrap: anywhere;
    }

    p {
        margin: 0 0 16px;
        font-size: 15px;
        color: var(--text-secondary);
        line-height: 1.7;
    }

    ul {
        margin: 0 0 16px;
        padding-left: 20px;
        display: flex;
        flex-direction: column;
        gap: 8px;
    }

    li {
        font-size: 15px;
        color: var(--text-secondary);
        line-height: 1.7;
    }

    a {
        color: var(--color-accent-bright);
        text-decoration: none;
    }

    a:hover {
        text-decoration: underline;
    }

    strong {
        color: var(--color-text);
        font-weight: 500;
    }
</style>
